(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[5 1 "// Frames and threads (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4; PYS7 (a)): a frame is a heap object holding a code"] [6 1 "// object's locals, cells, value stack and instruction index; the dispatch loop (eval.go) runs a"] [7 1 "// thread's frames without holding them on Go's stack, so a call from Python to Python is a new frame"] [8 1 "// and a return pops it, and a generator (PY5d) is a frame kept between resumptions."] [10 1 "// Frame is an executing code object (CPython's _PyInterpreterFrame and frame object)."] [13 21 "// the function run, nil for a module's or class's body"] [16 2 "// GlobalsMap is the globals when they are a dict subclass's instance (a function's from FunctionType(code, globals),"] [17 2 "// exec's and eval's; queue 205f), Globals its dict: LOAD_GLOBAL goes through its __getitem__; nil for a dict"] [19 19 "// the namespace of a module's or class's body (a module's is its Globals)"] [20 2 "// LocalsMap is a class body's namespace when __prepare__ returned a dict subclass: the name"] [21 2 "// operations go through its __getitem__, __setitem__ and __delitem__ (CPython's STORE_NAME on a"] [22 2 "// non-exact dict), Locals its dict. Added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b: enum's"] [23 2 "// EnumDict)."] [25 21 "// the fast locals; nil is unbound"] [26 21 "// the cells, then the free variables' cells"] [28 16 "// the next instruction"] [29 16 "// the instruction running, or the last run (f_lasti; tracebacks' line)"] [31 2 "// Suspended is set by a yield (PY5d): the frame returned a value but is kept to be resumed."] [33 17 "// the loop returns when this frame returns: it was called from Go"] [34 2 "// reraisedAt and reraisedLasti: a reraise N set the frame's reported instruction back to the raise it"] [35 2 "// re-raises (RERAISE's oparg: frame->instr_ptr), while its handler is still looked up at the reraise"] [37 2 "// escaped: a Python object may hold the frame (sys._getframe, a traceback, gi_frame, f_back, a signal"] [38 2 "// handler's argument), so it is never reused (202b: releaseFrame)"] [40 2 "// initSelf: the frame is an __init__ callInit runs for a class's call (queue 210), the instance made"] [42 2 "// gen is the generator, coroutine or async generator the frame is of (f_generator), nil for a call's"] [44 2 "// genAddr is the generator once it is tracked (Generator.track): the address alone, gen nil"] [46 2 "// views are the frame's rarely set views (f_locals' extra locals, f_trace; queue 219), nil until one is set: one"] [47 2 "// word in the frame, which every call allocates or clears"] [51 1 "// frameViews are a frame's views set from outside its code (queue 219)."] [53 2 "// extraLocals are the names f_locals' proxy stored that are none of the code's locals (PEP 667's f_extra_locals)"] [55 2 "// trace is f_trace, traceOpcodes f_trace_opcodes and noTraceLines f_trace_lines negated (the legacy tracer's,"] [56 2 "// trace.go; queue 219t)"] [61 1 "// view is f's views, made when absent."] [69 1 "// extra is f's extra locals, nil when none."] [77 1 "// escape marks f and the frames its f_back reaches escaped (a frame a Python object may hold; 202b)."] [84 1 "// The frames of a function's calls are reused (202b: CPython allocates its frames in a per-thread stack): a frame"] [85 1 "// that returned, made by newFrame for a function that is not a generator or a coroutine, and that no Python object"] [86 1 "// can reach (not escaped) goes back to its code's free list, at most frameFreeMax of them, cleared; newFrame takes"] [87 1 "// one from there before it allocates."] [98 1 "// releaseGenFrame is releaseFrame for the frame of a generator, coroutine or async generator that returned (gen.go's"] [99 1 "// resume; queue 210): its object no longer holds it."] [115 1 "// FrameType is the frame objects' type (sys._getframe, a traceback's tb_frame)."] [120 1 "// Line is the frame's current line (f_lineno), 0 when the code has no lines."] [123 1 "// ReportedLasti is f_lasti: Lasti, or after a reraise N there the instruction it re-raises from."] [148 1 "// popN pops n items and returns them in stack order (a view, valid until the next push)."] [159 1 "// Thread is a Python thread's state (PyThreadState): its current frame, the exception being"] [160 1 "// handled (sys.exception()), the call depth against the recursion limit. One thread runs at a time"] [161 1 "// (the GIL: PYS10 (a), PY6)."] [165 17 "// the exception being handled at this level (None outside handlers): the frame's or generator's slot"] [166 2 "// outer are the slots of the levels a running generator or coroutine was resumed from (CPython's exc_info"] [167 2 "// stack, gi_exc_state's previous_item): sys.exception() is the first that is not None (CurrentHandled)"] [170 2 "// cdepth is the C level's depth (PY7): the nested built-in calls CPython guards by _Py_EnterRecursiveCall"] [171 2 "// (comparison, repr, str, a tuple's hash, isinstance's and issubclass's recursions, the eval loop entered from"] [172 2 "// C), which CPython 3.14 measures on the machine's stack and pyi counts (enterRecursiveCall)"] [174 2 "// direct is the number of direct calls (callDirect: a compiled caller's Go frames under its compiled callee's"] [175 2 "// loop) nested on the thread's Go stack, at most directMax (queue 216d)"] [177 26 "// the containers being repr'd (Py_ReprEnter)"] [178 26 "// callStack's signal, reused (202b)"] [179 2 "// asyncio_running_loop and asyncio_running_task of the thread state (_asyncio, queue 224), nil when none"] [181 30 "// the current context (context.c: the thread state's), nil until first asked"] [184 1 "// CurrentHandled is the exception being handled (_PyErr_GetTopmostException): this level's slot, else the"] [185 1 "// first not None of the levels it was resumed from; None when none is."] [198 1 "// chainContext is _PyErr_SetObject's implicit chaining: exc's __context__ the exception being handled, a cycle"] [199 1 "// through exc in that chain cut first."] [217 10 "// a cycle not through exc"] [227 1 "// reprEnter is Py_ReprEnter: true when o is already being repr'd (a recursive container: \"[...]\")."] [239 1 "// reprLeave is Py_ReprLeave."] [242 1 "// The C level's stack (PY7). CPython 3.14 raises RecursionError \"Stack overflow (used N kB)WHERE\" when a guarded"] [243 1 "// built-in call (_Py_EnterRecursiveCall) finds the machine's stack past its soft limit; a Python frame does not use it."] [244 1 "// pyi's built-ins recurse on Go's stack, a goroutine's at most 1 GB, which a deep enough structure overflowed (a fatal"] [245 1 "// Go error: test_tuple's test_hash_deeply_nested, test_copy's reflexive comparisons, test_isinstance's recursions)."] [246 1 "// pyi counts the guarded levels instead, and Go's calls into the machine (Thread.run: the eval loop entered from C,"] [247 1 "// where \"\"): cStackLevels of them, cFrameBytes each as the message's nominal kB (about"] [248 1 "// CPython's 1 MB soft limit on Linux); CPython's own depth varies with the call (on Alpine aarch64 a tuple's hash"] [249 1 "// reaches 10,000 levels, its repr not)."] [255 1 "// enterRecursiveCall is _Py_EnterRecursiveCall(where): false, with the RecursionError, past the limit; else the"] [256 1 "// level is entered and leaveRecursiveCall leaves it."] [269 1 "// stackOverflow is _Py_CheckRecursiveCall's RecursionError."] [274 1 "// leaveRecursiveCall is _Py_LeaveRecursiveCall for enterRecursiveCall's thread."] [283 1 "// currentThread is the running thread (the GIL's holder)."] [286 1 "// unbound is the marker :load-fast-and-clear pushes for an unbound local (PEP 709)."] [293 1 "// newFrame makes the frame of a function's call with its arguments bound (CPython's"] [294 1 "// _PyEval_MakeFrameVector); args holds the positional then the keyword arguments."] [305 3 "// the fast locals and the value stack in one allocation (202b): the stack's room the most the code's"] [306 3 "// frames have needed (Code.stackHint, kept by runFrames at a return), so a call does not grow it from nothing"] [319 13 "// _tracemalloc's allocation (queue 220): the caller's, the callee not entered yet"] [334 1 "// bindArgs puts a call's arguments into the parameters' slots (positional, *args, keyword-only,"] [335 1 "// **kwargs, then the defaults), raising CPython's TypeErrors (Python/ceval.c's, with the qualified name)."] [339 20 "// every parameter given by position (queue 210: the common call, without the general path)"] [454 1 "// joinNames is CPython's list of names: 'a', 'a' and 'b', 'a', 'b', and 'c'."] [479 1 "// newGeneratorHook makes the generator, coroutine or async generator object of a call's frame (its"] [480 1 "// code flagged :generator or :coroutine): PY5d's gen.go sets it."] [483 1 "// callFunction calls a Python function from Go: a frame run by a nested loop to its return."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[79 6] [79 30] [152 12] [152 30] [190 27] [190 35] [191 21] [298 21] [311 47] [314 37] [370 21] [370 43] [382 15] [382 30] [393 26] [407 19] [407 41] [424 28] [424 41] [431 12] [431 25] [440 18] [440 40]]} (go/file "frame.go" :imports [

